metal189.page.post=Post-Processing
metal189.page.rt=Ray Tracing
metal189.page.input=Input
metal189.opt.shaders=Shaders
metal189.opt.shaders.desc=Switches between the vanilla-identical renderer and the advanced pipeline (lighting, shadows, water, sky and post-processing). Shortcut: K.
metal189.opt.ctrlClickRightClick=Ctrl+Click
metal189.opt.ctrlClickRightClick.desc=Left Click (default): Ctrl+click is an ordinary left click, so Ctrl-based controls work. Right Click: Ctrl+left click acts as a right click, as Minecraft's LWJGL does on macOS. No other mod is needed for either.
metal189.opt.ctrlClickRightClick.0=Left Click
metal189.opt.ctrlClickRightClick.1=Right Click
metal189.opt.shadows=Shadows
metal189.opt.shadows.desc=Sun and moon shadows from a shadow map.
metal189.opt.shadowResolution=Shadow Resolution
metal189.opt.shadowResolution.desc=Size of the shadow map. Higher is sharper and costs more GPU memory and time.
metal189.opt.shadowDistance=Shadow Distance
metal189.opt.shadowDistance.desc=How far from the camera the shadow map reaches. Shorter is sharper.
metal189.opt.playerShadow=First-Person Shadow
metal189.opt.playerShadow.desc=Your own player casts a shadow in first person, and appears in ray-traced reflections and occlusion.
metal189.opt.sunBrightness=Sun Brightness
metal189.opt.sunBrightness.desc=Strength of direct sunlight and moonlight.
metal189.opt.skyLightBrightness=Sky Light
metal189.opt.skyLightBrightness.desc=Strength of the light from the sky that fills shadows outdoors.
metal189.opt.blockLightBrightness=Block Light
metal189.opt.blockLightBrightness.desc=Brightness of torches, lamps, glowstone and other light sources.
metal189.opt.blockLightWarmth=Block Light Warmth
metal189.opt.blockLightWarmth.desc=Colour of block light: 0% is neutral white, 100% warm torch orange, 200% deep amber.
metal189.opt.minimumLight=Minimum Light
metal189.opt.minimumLight.desc=The faint light left in completely dark places, such as unlit caves.
metal189.opt.heldLight=Held Light
metal189.opt.heldLight.desc=Torches and other light sources in your hand light up their surroundings (and burning players glow).
metal189.opt.plantShadows=Plant Shadows
metal189.opt.plantShadows.desc=Grass, flowers, crops and other small plants cast shadows. Leaves always do.
metal189.opt.foliageTranslucency=Foliage Translucency
metal189.opt.foliageTranslucency.desc=Sunlight shining through leaves and plants: their shaded side glows, most of all when you look towards the sun through them.
metal189.opt.ssao=Ambient Occlusion
metal189.opt.ssao.desc=Screen-space ambient occlusion: soft darkening in corners and crevices.
metal189.opt.waving=Waving Foliage
metal189.opt.waving.desc=Leaves, grass, flowers and crops sway in the wind.
metal189.opt.autoExposure=Auto Exposure
metal189.opt.autoExposure.desc=Adapts the exposure to the scene brightness over time, like an eye or a camera.
metal189.opt.exposure=Exposure
metal189.opt.exposure.desc=Overall image brightness before tone mapping.
metal189.opt.pbr=PBR Materials
metal189.opt.pbr.desc=Uses the normal and specular textures of PBR resource packs (_n and _s files): surface detail, glossiness, metals and glowing parts. Packs without them are unaffected.
metal189.opt.pbrFormat=PBR Format
metal189.opt.pbrFormat.desc=How the pack's material textures are laid out. LabPBR is the current standard; SEUS is the older format (normal map as RGB, specular as smoothness/metalness/emission). Packs don't say which they use, so pick the one the pack documents.
metal189.opt.pbrFormat.0=LabPBR
metal189.opt.pbrFormat.1=SEUS (old)
metal189.opt.pbrNormalStrength=Normal Map Strength
metal189.opt.pbrNormalStrength.desc=How strongly the normal maps bend the lighting across a surface. 0% is flat.
metal189.opt.pbrSpecularStrength=Specular Strength
metal189.opt.pbrSpecularStrength.desc=Glossiness and reflectance from the specular maps. 0% makes every surface matte, above 100% shinier than the pack intends.
metal189.opt.pbrEmissionStrength=Emission Strength
metal189.opt.pbrEmissionStrength.desc=Brightness of the parts that the specular maps mark as glowing.
metal189.opt.pom=Parallax Occlusion
metal189.opt.pom.desc=Surfaces gain real-looking depth from the pack's height maps: bricks, cobblestone and ores stand out and hide each other at angles.
metal189.opt.pomDepth=Parallax Depth
metal189.opt.pomDepth.desc=How deep the deepest part of a texture goes, as a share of a block.
metal189.opt.pomQuality=Parallax Quality
metal189.opt.pomQuality.desc=Steps used to trace the height map. Higher is smoother at steep angles and costs more GPU time.
metal189.opt.pomQuality.0=Low
metal189.opt.pomQuality.1=Medium
metal189.opt.pomQuality.2=High
metal189.opt.pomQuality.3=Ultra
metal189.opt.pomDistance=Parallax Distance
metal189.opt.pomDistance.desc=Parallax is applied up to this distance and fades out before it.
metal189.opt.water=Water Effects
metal189.opt.water.desc=Waves, reflections, refraction and underwater fog. Off: water is drawn like other translucent blocks.
metal189.opt.waterStyle=Water Style
metal189.opt.waterStyle.desc=Smooth: detailed rolling waves. Pixel: the same waves in 16x16 steps, matching the block textures. Vanilla: a flat surface with the vanilla water texture.
metal189.opt.waterStyle.0=Smooth Waves
metal189.opt.waterStyle.1=Pixel Waves
metal189.opt.waterStyle.2=Vanilla Texture
metal189.opt.waterWaveStrength=Wave Strength
metal189.opt.waterWaveStrength.desc=How steep the waves are. 0% is perfectly still water.
metal189.opt.waterWaveSize=Wave Size
metal189.opt.waterWaveSize.desc=Scale of the wave pattern. Larger values give longer, broader waves.
metal189.opt.waterWaveSpeed=Wave Speed
metal189.opt.waterWaveSpeed.desc=How fast the waves travel. Longer waves always move faster than short ones.
metal189.opt.waterCalmIndoors=Calm Indoor Water
metal189.opt.waterCalmIndoors.desc=Water with no view of the sky (caves, houses) has smaller waves.
metal189.opt.waterRainRipples=Rain Ripples
metal189.opt.waterRainRipples.desc=Raindrops make expanding rings on water that is open to the sky.
metal189.opt.waterReflections=Reflections
metal189.opt.waterReflections.desc=Sky Only: water reflects the sky and the sun. Screen-Space: also what is on screen (trees, hills, mobs). Ray-traced reflections are on the Ray Tracing page.
metal189.opt.waterReflections.0=Sky Only
metal189.opt.waterReflections.1=Screen-Space
metal189.opt.waterReflectivity=Reflectivity
metal189.opt.waterReflectivity.desc=How much water reflects when you look straight down at it. Real water is 2%; more gives a mirror-like lake look. Reflections always grow towards grazing angles.
metal189.opt.waterSunReflection=Sun Reflection
metal189.opt.waterSunReflection.desc=Brightness of the sun and moon glinting on the waves.
metal189.opt.waterRefraction=Refraction
metal189.opt.waterRefraction.desc=How strongly the waves bend the view of what lies under the water.
metal189.opt.waterClarity=Water Clarity
metal189.opt.waterClarity.desc=How far you can see into water: the depth at which half of the light is absorbed.
metal189.opt.waterColorR=Water Color: Red
metal189.opt.waterColorR.desc=Red in the water's colour. Also changes which light the water absorbs: water that looks blue lets blue through.
metal189.opt.waterColorG=Water Color: Green
metal189.opt.waterColorG.desc=Green in the water's colour. Also changes which light the water absorbs.
metal189.opt.waterColorB=Water Color: Blue
metal189.opt.waterColorB.desc=Blue in the water's colour. Also changes which light the water absorbs.
metal189.opt.waterBiomeTint=Biome Water Color
metal189.opt.waterBiomeTint.desc=Tints water with its biome's water colour (in 1.8.9 only swamps have one).
metal189.opt.waterFoam=Shore Foam
metal189.opt.waterFoam.desc=White foam where the water meets the shore or objects. Above 100% the foam is brighter.
metal189.opt.waterFoamWidth=Foam Width
metal189.opt.waterFoamWidth.desc=How far from the shore the foam reaches.
metal189.opt.underwaterVisibility=Underwater Visibility
metal189.opt.underwaterVisibility.desc=How far you can see while underwater: the distance at which fog hides half of the view.
metal189.opt.underwaterDistortion=Underwater Distortion
metal189.opt.underwaterDistortion.desc=A slow, slight wobble of the view while your head is under water.
metal189.opt.underwaterOverlay=Underwater Overlay
metal189.opt.underwaterOverlay.desc=Vanilla's wavy water texture over the screen while your head is under water. Works with shaders on or off.
metal189.opt.hideUnderwaterParticles=Hide Underwater Particles
metal189.opt.hideUnderwaterParticles.desc=Hides vanilla's tiny particles that float inside water. With shaders they would show through the water surface as sharp squares.
metal189.opt.sky=Physical Sky
metal189.opt.sky.desc=Atmospheric scattering sky with a sun and moon, instead of vanilla's sky colours.
metal189.opt.clouds=Volumetric Clouds
metal189.opt.clouds.desc=Ray-marched 3D clouds that cast shadows, instead of vanilla's flat clouds.
metal189.opt.volumetrics=Light Shafts
metal189.opt.volumetrics.desc=Sunlight scattering in the air: visible shafts of light through gaps (needs Shadows).
metal189.opt.cloudCoverage=Cloud Coverage
metal189.opt.cloudCoverage.desc=How much of the sky the volumetric clouds cover. Rain still brings more.
metal189.opt.cloudSpeed=Cloud Speed
metal189.opt.cloudSpeed.desc=How fast the clouds drift.
metal189.opt.hazeDensity=Haze
metal189.opt.hazeDensity.desc=Atmospheric haze over distant terrain and in light shafts.
metal189.opt.starBrightness=Star Brightness
metal189.opt.starBrightness.desc=Brightness of the stars at night.
metal189.opt.vignette=Vignette
metal189.opt.vignette.desc=Darkening towards the corners of the screen.
metal189.opt.sharpening=Sharpening
metal189.opt.sharpening.desc=Restores texture detail that temporal anti-aliasing softens.
metal189.opt.saturation=Saturation
metal189.opt.saturation.desc=Colour intensity of the final image. 0% is black and white.
metal189.opt.contrast=Contrast
metal189.opt.contrast.desc=Difference between dark and bright parts of the final image.
metal189.opt.taa=Temporal AA
metal189.opt.taa.desc=Temporal anti-aliasing with sharpening: smooth edges and stable details. Also denoises reflections and ray tracing.
metal189.opt.bloom=Bloom
metal189.opt.bloom.desc=Bright light bleeds into its surroundings.
metal189.opt.bloomStrength=Bloom Strength
metal189.opt.bloomStrength.desc=Intensity of the bloom glow.
metal189.opt.rtShadows=RT Shadows
metal189.opt.rtShadows.desc=Exact ray-traced terrain shadows over the whole loaded world (hardware ray tracing).
metal189.opt.rtReflections=RT Reflections
metal189.opt.rtReflections.desc=Ray-traced reflections on water and smooth surfaces, including things off screen.
metal189.opt.rtAmbientOcclusion=RT Ambient Occlusion
metal189.opt.rtAmbientOcclusion.desc=Ray-traced ambient occlusion (replaces screen-space ambient occlusion).
metal189.opt.rtGlobalIllumination=RT Global Illumination
metal189.opt.rtGlobalIllumination.desc=One bounce of ray-traced indirect light: sky light and sunlight reflected off nearby surfaces.
metal189.opt.rtEntities=RT Entities
metal189.opt.rtEntities.desc=Mobs, players and block entities in ray-traced reflections, ambient occlusion and global illumination.
metal189.msg.on=Shaders enabled
metal189.msg.off=Shaders disabled
